<!--
  Adaptive icon foreground layer — the brand "stacked-dashes" glyph, white on
  transparent (CLAUDE.md "Design System & Visual Identity": light-mode logo =
  gradient background + white stacked-dashes icon).

  Port of the iOS AppIcon glyph (three horizontal rounded bars, decreasing
  width, left-aligned) measured off
  apps/ios/Meeshy/Assets.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset/Icon-Light-1024x1024.png
  (bar bounding boxes in source px: [222,344]-[801,423], [222,472]-[701,551],
  [222,600]-[601,679] on a 1024x1024 canvas, corner radius = half height on
  every bar). Scaled 108/1024 onto the adaptive-icon viewport then shrunk by
  0.85 so every bar corner stays inside the 66dp safe-zone circle (max corner
  distance from center ~30dp, vs. the 33dp safe radius) — see
  apps/android/scripts/generate_legacy_launcher_icons.py for the full
  derivation, shared verbatim with the legacy PNG fallbacks so the vector and
  raster renders never drift.
-->
